WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.260
Want a soda?

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:02.620
This'll cost you

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:04.240
more in Philadelphia because

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:06.160
politicians there

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:07.581
voted to tax these.

00:00:07.581 --> 00:00:08.820
Ayes are 13,

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.120
the nays are 4.

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.480
Listen to the applause.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:15.720
The sugar sweet beverage tax.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.572
There was more applause when the bill was signed.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:20.520
The politicians said the tax will

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.640
fund early childhood education.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:24.700
This would be great for this community

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:26.100
and to help a lot of families.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.500
But store owners say,

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:28.440
"It's a bad tax."

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:29.300
Melvin Robinson,

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.240
who runs Bruno's Pizza says

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:32.658
the soda tax is killing

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:33.980
his business.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.380
What do your customers say?

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:36.323
What'd they say?

00:00:36.323 --> 00:00:37.620
They're not buying it.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.140
I refuse

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:40.900
to buy soda in Philadelphia.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:43.200
Well, a 20 ounce soda almost 3 dollars.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.272
So instead of buying at Bruno's,

00:00:45.272 --> 00:00:47.080
they cross the street

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.380
because Bruno's is located

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:49.900
right on the outer edge

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:50.920
of Philly.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.580
So I gotta get a soda or a juice.

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:53.500
I'll go

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:54.720
right across the street.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.000
Right. These customers

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.800
just cross the street,

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.380
save a buck.

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:01.619
When I want something to drink I go right there.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:02.620
But he comes here

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:03.580
for the pizza.

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:04.080
Yeah yeah,

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.520
they got the best slice in town.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:06.954
But the soda tax still

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.320
punishes Melvin.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:10.900
This happens whenever local governments impose

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:12.320
special new taxes.

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:13.300
Like who

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.940
should pay three dollars for a drink

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:16.900
that they used to get for 99 cents?

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.380
If customers can escape,

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:19.260
they will.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:21.622
Do the politicians think about that ?

00:01:21.622 --> 00:01:23.240
So a buck more

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:24.260
for one of these?

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:25.480
It definitely is more,

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:26.420
but it's for

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:28.480
what we feel is a good reason

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:29.480
for a good cause.

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:31.500
City Councilman William Greenlee says

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:34.120
Philadelphia needs the tax money.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:35.788
Nothing else that we could come up with

00:01:35.788 --> 00:01:38.240
could raise that kind of funding.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:41.160
But soda taxes are

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:43.900
disproportionately paid by poor people.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:45.380
Even so-called progressives

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:47.780
campaigned against this tax.

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:50.540
You don't have to fund child care

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:54.280
on the backs of the poorest people in this city.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:57.140
That's a regressive way to raise funds.

00:01:57.140 --> 00:01:58.920
It hits the poor most.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:00.240
Even Bernie Sanders

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:02.700
opposes this tax.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:05.120
I didn't know Bernie opposed it but okay.

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:07.340
Remember we're raising enough money

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:09.860
to put 2700 kids in

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:12.680
Pre-K and to open 11 community schools.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:14.240
The pizza parlor's customers

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:15.628
didn't think their taxes

00:02:15.628 --> 00:02:17.040
were being well-spent.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:18.220
Preschool?

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:19.660
I doubt that very much.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:21.680
The mayor says he's helping people.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:22.620
He ain't helping me.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:23.420
He's tearing me up.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:26.300
Meanwhile,

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:29.020
taxes create unintended consequences.

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:31.640
Soda sales are way down.

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:34.420
But sales of more harmful products are up.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.860
Now some people are buying more liquor,

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:38.920
less Coke, more liquor.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:39.940
I don't know about that

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:41.640
because we have a liquor tax too so....

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:45.640
Politicians love taxes on unhealthy things

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:46.980
and so do the media.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:50.060
They applauded when Denmark taxed fatty food.

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:51.960
Denmark has decided to implement

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:53.820
what they're calling a fat tax.

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:55.620
Basically you go to the supermarket,

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:58.540
you buy a food that has above a certain level of fat,

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:00.120
they charge you extra.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:00.700
Alright,

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:02.020
do we feel good about this, Doc?

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:02.980
Absolutely.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:05.340
But Danes just crossed the border

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:07.000
to shop in other countries.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.240
Within a year,

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:10.160
Denmark repealed its fat tax.

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:12.460
But Philadelphia isn't repealing

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:13.334
anything.

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:15.500
People in this town already pay

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.060
44 taxes.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:18.533
State income tax,

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:19.700
sales tax,

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:21.920
cigarette and alcohol taxes.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:24.420
Philadelphia has a very high income tax

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:26.260
compared to other places.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:27.980
How can you not have enough money?

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:28.480
The wage tax is high.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:29.620
You should be rolling in money.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:30.840
Oh I don't know about that.

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:32.600
But there's a lot to do out there, John.

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:33.660
4 million for the

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.540
Office of Arts and Culture

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:36.420
Mm-hmm.

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:39.177
Funded two sessions of dance instruction,

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:40.880
teach youth empowerment,

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:42.860
social issues through hip hop.

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:43.752
Office of Arts and Culture

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:45.860
does a very good job in the city of Philadelphia.

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:47.760
Like we need that.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:48.960
Like we need that.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.720
They're funding the Arts.

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:52.240
What Arts?

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:54.020
People trying to live.

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:55.860
Politician says "We gotta raise money."

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:57.540
Stop stealing.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:58.680
That would be nice.

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:00.460
I don't know that he's stealing, but

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:03.900
he pays himself 121 thousand bucks a year.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:05.020
Wow.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:07.880
You make $121,000 a year,

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.225
three times what the

00:04:09.225 --> 00:04:10.360
median income

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:12.160
of what your citizens make.

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:14.180
Well, I don't think that's terribly unusual

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:16.000
for elected officials.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.700
Sadly he's right.

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:20.200
Politicians routinely make much more

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:22.460
than the people they allegedly serve.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:24.280
A lot of citizens should make more money,

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:25.280
you know.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:26.400
Well they can't make more money

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:27.627
when you're taxing them to death.

00:04:27.627 --> 00:04:29.440
Well, I don't think we're taxing them to death.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:31.741
The politicians

00:04:31.741 --> 00:04:33.560
always want more

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:35.260
and the restaurants,

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:36.540
they just have to pay.

